think ALES214's own design read named the honest next move: open a fresh Lotus family rather than another reverb knob. Lindy-first crux-first: the most durable thing the suite lacks is a container — a way for any of the 200-plus effects to leave the bench as a real file.
think Chose the canonical RIFF/WAVE mono 16-bit PCM container (lotus/wav.rye) — a public, unencumbered, 30-year-old interchange format; the crux that opens the rest (every effect gains export/import for free) and the highest-Lindy surface in the suite.
think Carried ALES0 wire.rye's discipline verbatim: verify-before-trust decode with TWO independent gates — the size chain proving the container self-consistent, the audio border (data_size % 2 == 0) proving it sample-aligned so no torn half-sample reaches a timeline.
think Encode/decode over caller-provided buffers (no giant fixed arrays), every bound named at the edge; ≥2 asserts per fn with // invariant, named errors, no bare memcpy (writeInt loops), opening triad present.
obs GREEN on metal: ales_wav_witness proves byte-for-byte round-trip, canonical header, empty buffer, PartialSample at the audio border, and 15 named faults each refusing before a sample crosses. tame_style_check GREEN (bans clean; wav.rye carries asserts, not in the zero-assert ratchet list).
obs Honest scope held: a byte container only — no real file opened, no DAC, no acoustic/electrical fact asserted, no network, no keys, no funds. No custody gate touched.
